    "name": "Fire Tester firmware 0.1.688b"
  },
  "notes": "Adds a bounded BLETX DUMP diagnostic for the current and previous Twin connection: exact local no-response write result, first/latest failure time, last locally accepted write time, and free packet buffers at failure. The existing seven-/nine-byte state payload, cadence and Twin timeout are preserved. Local acceptance does not prove remote receipt.\n\nIncludes a host-only passive LED watcher with an explicit read allowlist, fresh identity checks, finite evidence bounds and cleanup reporting. It does not send Search, radio-control or actuator commands. The allowed LED snapshot keeps the USB diagnostic data session alive.\n\nThis release strengthens evidence for an observed intermittent BLE transport failure; it does not claim that its root cause is already fixed. Existing flashlight learning records are preserved. Full physical device QA remains ongoing.\n",
